// Windows child #4 (companion to ../mainwindows.bit, #5782): sleeps well
// past the parent's bounded timeout, to exercise the `-2` timeout/reap path.
// `timeSleepNs` is a predeclared builtin (compiler/symbols.bit), matching
// `_tests_/bit/windowssmoke.bit`'s own child — deliberately not `std/time`'s
// `sleep`, so this program pulls in no extra imports.
fn main() {
  timeSleepNs(30000000000) // 30s
}
